WEBVTT

00:32.198 --> 00:36.953
THE PRACTICAL GUIDE TO LOVE

00:37.036 --> 00:38.829
- Hello, nice to meet you.
- Hi.

00:38.913 --> 00:40.081
- Nice to meet you.
- Looking forward to meeting you.

00:40.164 --> 00:41.999
- Is this Ms. Lee?
- Hey.

00:48.339 --> 00:49.423
Are you okay?

00:50.550 --> 00:51.717
Are you hurt?

00:51.801 --> 00:53.844
- Hello.
- Ms. Ui-yeong?

00:53.928 --> 00:55.137
- A friend...
- Looking for a date?

00:55.221 --> 00:58.266
Are they all asking me out
on a blind date?

01:00.643 --> 01:02.770
- What in the world is going on?
- Exactly.

01:03.771 --> 01:04.772
Sorry?

01:06.399 --> 01:09.610
THE PRACTICAL GUIDE TO LOVE
EPISODE 3

01:12.238 --> 01:13.364
Have I been hacked?

01:13.698 --> 01:15.825
Has my number been leaked?
From my phone company?

01:15.908 --> 01:17.076
Maybe from online shopping?

01:17.535 --> 01:19.453
YOON BAK:
HELLO, NICE TO MEET YOU. I'M YOON BAK

01:19.537 --> 01:21.831
- Hello, nice to meet you. I'm Yoon Bak.
- Who is this?

01:22.498 --> 01:24.083
I'M YUK JUN-SEO

01:24.166 --> 01:25.501
I'm Yuk Jun-seo.

01:25.585 --> 01:28.337
I'm Lee Ho-gwang.
I'm a singer and stage performer.

01:28.421 --> 01:29.839
When are you free this week?

01:29.922 --> 01:31.007
Hello, Ui-yeong.

01:31.090 --> 01:33.759
I'm Kim Do-yun,
the brother of your dermatologist.

01:33.843 --> 01:34.844
What's going on?

01:34.927 --> 01:37.305
Hello, I'm Song Ji-hun, Na-hyeon's friend.

01:37.388 --> 01:39.265
I sent him your photo,
and he's interested.

01:39.390 --> 01:40.975
He's super successful as a teacher.

01:41.183 --> 01:42.935
- I'll give him your number.
- Wait!

01:43.603 --> 01:44.729
I'll see who I know.

01:44.812 --> 01:46.188
I gave your number to a friend.

01:46.272 --> 01:47.690
- Random, but sure.
- I'll share your number.

01:47.773 --> 01:49.650
Okay, I'll look into it.

01:53.237 --> 01:54.989
LEE DA-EUN FROM CLASS OF 2013

01:56.490 --> 01:57.950
YOU KNOW A GOOD GUY? I'M SO LONELY

01:59.619 --> 02:00.703
CAN YOU SET ME UP WITH A GUY?

02:00.786 --> 02:02.079
CAN YOU FIND ME A BOYFRIEND?

02:04.081 --> 02:05.791
PASTE

02:05.875 --> 02:07.793
FIND A GUY FOR ME! YOU KNOW ANYONE NICE?

02:14.133 --> 02:16.636
You've got to be kidding me!

02:18.429 --> 02:19.930
You're crazy!

02:24.644 --> 02:26.520
- I'm home.
- Hey.

02:28.397 --> 02:30.024
- Gosh, my shoulders.
- Oh, man.

02:30.816 --> 02:32.026
Hey

02:35.363 --> 02:36.947
what's all this?

02:37.615 --> 02:40.368
I thought you liked
wearing your uniform to work every day.

02:41.285 --> 02:42.370
Are you not feeling well?

02:43.579 --> 02:45.414
You don't have a fever.

02:45.498 --> 02:47.708
Stop it. That's not it.

02:47.792 --> 02:49.710
Next time I'm drunk,
just turn my phone off.

02:49.794 --> 02:51.003
Or chop my hands off.

02:51.087 --> 02:53.047
- Not your credit card?
- Hey.

02:53.130 --> 02:55.633
They're not just any clothes.
They're my armor.

02:56.092 --> 02:58.386
Come on. Look at this.

02:58.761 --> 03:01.889
What armor is this soft and fluffy?

03:02.223 --> 03:04.392
What about this?

03:04.892 --> 03:06.227
Is this camouflage cream?

03:07.269 --> 03:09.855
- My goodness.
- You'd better not use any.

03:10.439 --> 03:11.565
It's all mine.

03:12.483 --> 03:13.693
Geez.

03:17.738 --> 03:20.866
This hides my flaws
and makes me feel confident.

03:21.283 --> 03:22.410
I'd say that's an armor.

03:26.414 --> 03:27.415
Alright.

03:39.051 --> 03:41.095
It may have been a drunken wish

03:41.303 --> 03:42.847
but a chance is a chance.

03:47.226 --> 03:49.562
There's only a 1% chance now

03:49.937 --> 03:52.440
but I'll get to know them
and find my best match.

03:53.149 --> 03:54.817
I'LL GIVE YOUR NUMBER TO HIM

03:55.067 --> 03:56.360
OH, GOSH... I'LL LOOK FOR ONE

03:56.444 --> 03:59.280
- I'll look for one.
- Even your texts sound drunk.

03:59.363 --> 04:00.614
- Let's grab lunch sometime.
- Random

04:00.698 --> 04:02.241
- but sure.
- Ui-yeong, are you drunk?

04:02.324 --> 04:03.868
If I knew a good guy,
I wouldn't be single.

04:03.951 --> 04:06.162
- Do you know anyone?
- Those are just empty words.

04:06.579 --> 04:07.580
I'll look for one.

04:07.663 --> 04:09.248
Can I ask you a favor, too?

04:09.331 --> 04:11.834
Can you book a wedding consultation
at your hotel?

04:11.917 --> 04:14.378
Of course, it's all about give and take.

04:14.962 --> 04:17.339
Of course. When's a good time for you?

04:19.300 --> 04:21.218
HELLO, NICE TO MEET YOU. I'M YOON BAK

04:21.302 --> 04:23.304
Hello, I'm Lee Ui-yeong.

04:23.763 --> 04:25.639
Are you free this Saturday?

04:27.516 --> 04:28.559
Alright, then.

04:28.642 --> 04:29.894
YOON BAK, 37, AT 1:30 P.M.

04:29.977 --> 04:32.313
MATH INSTRUCTOR

04:33.022 --> 04:34.315
YOON BAK, 37, MATH INSTRUCTOR,
AT 1:30 P.M.

04:38.694 --> 04:40.613
Good morning.

04:42.656 --> 04:44.492
Is the other one for me?

04:44.575 --> 04:47.787
No, they're both mine. I need to wake up.

04:47.953 --> 04:49.580
Hmm? Did you not sleep well?

04:50.372 --> 04:51.373
You look great to me.

04:53.292 --> 04:54.835
Your calendar is so full!

04:56.879 --> 04:58.672
They're all blind dates!

04:59.173 --> 05:00.174
KIM DO-HA, 38, SONGWRITER, AT 7 P.M.

05:00.925 --> 05:03.677
LEE SEONG-JAE, 31, DESIGNER,
AT 7:30 A.M.

05:03.761 --> 05:05.971
People go on blind dates before work?

05:06.055 --> 05:07.556
Yeah, I'm one of them.

05:08.390 --> 05:10.226
There was no other time. I had no choice.

05:12.186 --> 05:15.856
I was just determined to fix
what I'd done last night

05:15.940 --> 05:17.399
but this is going too far, right?

05:17.483 --> 05:18.651
Seeing just one is tiring.

05:18.734 --> 05:20.611
And this isn't even polite, right?

05:21.779 --> 05:23.697
You're not even dating anyone yet.

05:23.781 --> 05:26.826
It's not rude,
as long as you do your best on every date.

05:27.618 --> 05:29.662
Don't worry. Just go for it.

05:29.912 --> 05:32.832
Most importantly, if you cancel now

05:34.083 --> 05:35.292
people won't set you up.

05:35.376 --> 05:37.378
That's one less matchmaker you'll have.

05:39.755 --> 05:41.048
That can't happen.

05:47.680 --> 05:48.681
DEERFIDDICH, PREMIUM WHISKEY BRAND

05:48.764 --> 05:53.936
Our hotel is hosting
the 100th anniversary event

05:54.019 --> 05:56.230
for Deerfiddich
from the middle of next month.

05:58.399 --> 06:00.359
A big project now, of all times?

06:00.442 --> 06:01.777
The event is three weeks long?

06:01.861 --> 06:03.654
Yes, we'll set up a pop-up store

06:03.737 --> 06:07.700
to display the whiskey
and hold tasting sessions in the lobby.

06:07.783 --> 06:11.662
The brand has asked us
to plan and organize all of it.

06:11.745 --> 06:12.913
- I see.
- I see.

06:13.831 --> 06:16.375
Why don't we use temporary walls

06:16.458 --> 06:18.460
to create a "shop-in-shop" style setup?

06:18.586 --> 06:20.713
We could put up a sign
and hire a bartender

06:20.796 --> 06:22.631
to create a Scottish-style whiskey bar

06:22.715 --> 06:24.466
in our hotel lobby.

06:24.717 --> 06:25.718
That's a great idea.

06:25.801 --> 06:27.720
We'll develop that idea.

06:27.803 --> 06:29.847
Purchasing, please look for a company

06:29.930 --> 06:31.473
- that could set up the shop.
- Okay.

06:31.557 --> 06:34.018
Facilities, please help us
when we set up the shop.

06:34.101 --> 06:35.769
Yes, you can leave that to us.

06:36.520 --> 06:38.314
Can we have a glass, too?

06:54.246 --> 06:55.247
Please.

06:58.375 --> 07:03.339
PURCHASING TEAM OFFICE

07:09.511 --> 07:12.431
You know
how Ui-yeong's been working nonstop?

07:12.681 --> 07:14.975
She's been there to solve every issue.

07:15.059 --> 07:16.101
Yes.

07:16.185 --> 07:18.729
So, let her live her life now.

07:18.812 --> 07:20.689
We can manage with what we've learned.

07:20.773 --> 07:23.233
You should prove yourself
before the internship's over.

07:23.317 --> 07:25.569
Yes, I'm ready to work really hard.

07:26.362 --> 07:27.363
Right on!

07:29.073 --> 07:30.074
- Here.
- Thank you.

07:32.743 --> 07:35.245
Sae-byeok, are you free tonight?

07:35.371 --> 07:36.664
- Can we talk?
- Alright!

07:37.539 --> 07:39.667
Should we look for designers after dinner?

07:39.750 --> 07:41.543
- Yes!
- Alright, cheers.

07:55.140 --> 07:56.183
You look great.

08:00.938 --> 08:01.939
Looks delicious.

08:05.234 --> 08:06.527
What do you do for a living?

08:11.323 --> 08:13.158
I learned from the countless first dates

08:13.492 --> 08:16.745
that the world is big,
and everyone's so different.

08:16.870 --> 08:18.580
None of the guys I met were

08:18.831 --> 08:21.792
even slightly similar.

08:22.334 --> 08:24.336
Everyone was

08:24.420 --> 08:26.714
- a universe like no other.
- Nice to meet you.

08:26.797 --> 08:28.841
You know me, right? I'm Yoon Bak.

08:28.924 --> 08:32.011
YOON BAK, 37, STAR MATH INSTRUCTOR

08:38.475 --> 08:39.727
You're already done eating.

08:39.810 --> 08:41.520
Would you like another soup?

08:41.603 --> 08:43.063
Are you already taking care of me?

08:43.147 --> 08:44.314
That was unexpected.

08:45.024 --> 08:46.025
Sorry?

08:46.108 --> 08:47.192
Just kidding.

08:47.317 --> 08:49.236
I usually eat my meals in a meeting

08:49.319 --> 08:50.612
so I always eat fast.

08:51.071 --> 08:53.282
I see.

08:54.033 --> 08:55.325
You must be so busy.

08:55.409 --> 08:57.911
I hear your classes are so popular.

08:57.995 --> 08:59.913
Is that what you really want to know?

08:59.997 --> 09:01.582
Aren't you just wondering

09:01.665 --> 09:04.043
if I'll have time to date
and take care of you?

09:04.126 --> 09:05.419
Oh, well...

09:07.713 --> 09:09.548
Do you have time?

09:09.715 --> 09:11.341
Time is gold to me.

09:11.425 --> 09:13.510
It must be at least silver or bronze
to you, too.

09:13.594 --> 09:15.846
We're here to meet
and listen to each other

09:15.929 --> 09:18.140
so what do you think happens next?

09:20.768 --> 09:22.019
What's going to happen?

09:23.270 --> 09:24.897
We know how it'll go.

09:25.939 --> 09:28.275
- You can be my girlfriend.
- What?

09:28.358 --> 09:30.569
If you just want to date,
I'll be a boyfriend.

09:30.652 --> 09:32.613
If you want to get married,
I'll be a husband.

09:32.696 --> 09:34.239
No need to think about anything.

09:34.323 --> 09:36.158
Just use me. I'll let you.

09:36.784 --> 09:38.619
That's what this is about. It's simple.

09:38.702 --> 09:41.747
He flirts like he's lecturing
a high school senior.

09:41.830 --> 09:44.458
I hear you love to work out.

09:44.541 --> 09:46.001
Are you okay with eating carbs?

09:46.085 --> 09:49.171
Yes, I prefer eating more of it
to fuel my workouts.

09:49.254 --> 09:51.632
YUK JUN-SEO, 29, FORMER UDT MEMBER
AND REHAB TRAINER

09:51.840 --> 09:52.925
I see.

09:53.884 --> 09:57.096
What's your priority in a relationship?

09:57.179 --> 09:58.263
Eating.

09:58.347 --> 10:00.140
Having different tastes is noticeable

10:00.224 --> 10:01.600
at every meal.

10:02.267 --> 10:04.144
Do you like to eat?

10:04.353 --> 10:06.980
Yes, I love to eat. I'm not picky, either.

10:08.315 --> 10:10.442
I have so many restaurants
I want to check out.

10:10.651 --> 10:12.945
We could even go to a few today.

10:13.362 --> 10:14.404
This is exciting.

10:15.614 --> 10:16.949
"A few"?

10:21.912 --> 10:22.913
Tacos!

10:32.923 --> 10:33.924
Bagels!

10:35.175 --> 10:36.176
Gelato!

10:38.720 --> 10:39.763
Desserts!

10:47.771 --> 10:51.483
I feel like my stomach will explode
if I see him again.

11:01.493 --> 11:04.246
I was going to pay for the coffee.

11:04.329 --> 11:07.624
Don't say that

11:07.708 --> 11:10.127
LEE HO-GWANG, 36, MUSICAL ACTOR

11:10.752 --> 11:15.424
You gave me the greatest gift,
a pricelessly perfect day.

11:15.841 --> 11:17.092
You're my muse

11:18.677 --> 11:19.803
from today on.

11:21.430 --> 11:22.431
Your muse?

11:22.514 --> 11:25.517
Like Christine
in "The Phantom of the Opera."

11:26.268 --> 11:27.477
"The Phantom of the Opera"?

11:29.021 --> 11:32.900
Ho-gwang, it's getting late.
I'd better get home.

11:32.983 --> 11:34.693
I live right here, so I can go alone.

11:34.860 --> 11:37.196
No

11:38.280 --> 11:40.240
I don't want you to walk alone
in the dark.

11:41.158 --> 11:42.951
I can already sense the dark souls

11:43.410 --> 11:45.287
trying to steal you away, my sunshine.

11:45.370 --> 11:49.208
The man who called me his muse,
Christine, and sunshine

11:49.291 --> 11:50.584
and got overly protective...

11:50.667 --> 11:51.960
She told you to go. Leave.

11:52.044 --> 11:54.463
She doesn't seem to want to show you
where she lives.

11:54.546 --> 11:57.299
Who are you, ma'am?

11:57.382 --> 11:58.884
Why are you intruding?

11:58.967 --> 12:00.636
Me? Her mom.

12:00.802 --> 12:03.722
Jesus Christ Superstar!

12:03.847 --> 12:05.766
No, not a superstar. Her mom.

12:05.849 --> 12:08.060
It's like you're not even listening.

12:08.143 --> 12:11.396
He was tragically defeated
by the nemesis of romance.

12:11.480 --> 12:13.607
Mother

12:13.732 --> 12:15.067
My mother

12:15.150 --> 12:17.527
Your mother

12:25.911 --> 12:30.624
Please join me in prayer
to give thanks for our date.

12:30.707 --> 12:33.877
This man doesn't go on dates on Sundays
because that's the Lord's day.

12:33.961 --> 12:35.337
Do you also like drinking?

12:35.420 --> 12:36.964
Why can't you just drink at home?

12:37.047 --> 12:39.049
Why do women have to go out for drinks?

12:39.132 --> 12:42.052
This one still seemed
like he wasn't over his ex.

12:43.011 --> 12:44.972
Sure, you can have different tastes.

12:45.055 --> 12:48.183
But why would you pour the sauce
without asking the other person first?

12:48.267 --> 12:49.977
That says a lot about who you are.

12:50.060 --> 12:53.480
A man who can't stand inconsiderate people
who pour the sauce without asking.

12:53.563 --> 12:55.148
- Please be my girlfriend!
- Please be my girlfriend!

12:55.232 --> 12:56.775
- Please.
- Please be my girlfriend.

12:56.858 --> 12:57.901
- Please!
- Please!

12:57.985 --> 13:00.362
The problem is, among all those men

13:00.779 --> 13:02.864
none of them were my type.

13:20.465 --> 13:22.884
Ui-yeong!

13:22.968 --> 13:24.803
Where are you going?

13:24.886 --> 13:27.889
Ui-yeong! I love you!

13:28.223 --> 13:30.017
Stop right there!

13:30.100 --> 13:31.310
- Ui-yeong!
- Ui-yeong!

13:31.393 --> 13:32.477
Ui-yeong!

13:45.949 --> 13:48.452
I said you passed as my girlfriend
because I like you.

13:48.535 --> 13:50.287
Let's get more good food next time.

13:50.370 --> 13:52.039
Your mother is so charismatic.

13:52.122 --> 13:53.123
When we're out...

13:53.206 --> 13:55.500
We're heading to the hotel now. See you!

13:56.168 --> 13:57.336
Oh, I'm late!

14:11.433 --> 14:12.434
Tae-seop.

14:17.939 --> 14:18.982
Tae-seop.

14:28.825 --> 14:29.826
Ui-yeong!

14:37.084 --> 14:38.710
I thought she said she'd text me.

14:39.127 --> 14:41.004
Did her other date go well?

14:44.049 --> 14:46.218
DIRECTOR AT HOUSE OF ANIMALS

14:50.639 --> 14:51.681
Yes, Director?

14:52.933 --> 14:55.769
I can't believe you're getting married.
Congratulations.

14:55.852 --> 14:57.062
Thank you.

14:57.270 --> 14:59.064
It's great that you work at a hotel.

14:59.147 --> 15:00.148
It's nothing.

15:00.232 --> 15:03.485
By the way, all consultations were full
on the weekend.

15:03.568 --> 15:05.320
They made a special slot for you

15:05.529 --> 15:07.864
so don't tell anyone else, okay?

15:08.573 --> 15:09.866
Don't worry.

15:09.950 --> 15:13.120
Who can even afford to get married
at such a nice hotel?

15:14.704 --> 15:17.874
You two are so different.

15:18.083 --> 15:19.376
That's why we get along.

15:19.584 --> 15:21.962
We did a group project in college

15:22.087 --> 15:25.549
and she prepared everything
for the presentation and the assignment

15:25.632 --> 15:27.426
in exchange for 100,000 won from me.

15:27.926 --> 15:29.803
- And we got...
- A-plus.

15:30.637 --> 15:33.723
Nobody valued me like you did.

15:34.558 --> 15:37.477
How can you still be single
when you're so smart?

15:38.270 --> 15:39.354
- Honey.
- Yeah?

15:39.438 --> 15:42.482
Don't you know anyone
you can set her up with?

15:42.774 --> 15:44.484
- Hmm?
- Did you think of any?

15:44.568 --> 15:46.361
I told you to think of some!

15:46.445 --> 15:48.196
Hey, you're making him uncomfortable.

15:48.280 --> 15:49.906
It's fine.

15:49.990 --> 15:51.450
Come on. Find someone.

15:51.533 --> 15:52.784
Ms. Lee?

15:52.868 --> 15:54.077
Mr. Eun!

15:54.828 --> 15:57.289
I'm Eun Jeong-seok,
the General Manager at The Hills.

15:57.539 --> 16:00.917
I'll take you to the banquet room,
where the Wedding Manager is.

16:01.001 --> 16:02.252
You can leave it to me now.

16:02.335 --> 16:03.336
Please treat her well.

16:03.420 --> 16:04.880
We'll provide the best service.

16:07.507 --> 16:08.508
Text me later.

16:11.178 --> 16:12.179
Ui-yeong!

16:13.680 --> 16:14.806
What are you doing here?

16:17.809 --> 16:21.104
So, you were checking out of here

16:21.354 --> 16:23.315
and ran into Mr. Eun?

16:23.690 --> 16:25.734
What if people talk about you?

16:25.817 --> 16:28.153
What can I do?
I have to use my employee discount.

16:28.820 --> 16:32.115
And why should people be talking
about grown-ups having sex?

16:32.199 --> 16:33.742
Do you not do it?

16:34.451 --> 16:35.619
You're something else.

16:37.996 --> 16:42.000
But you know,
dating is starting to get boring.

16:42.876 --> 16:44.419
There's always a pattern.

16:44.628 --> 16:47.464
We meet, introduce ourselves,
eat a meal, and have sex.

16:47.547 --> 16:49.007
I can't meet a guy twice.

16:49.090 --> 16:50.759
Should I just become a celebrity fan?

16:51.510 --> 16:53.094
Why does that sound relatable?

16:58.600 --> 17:00.852
I said you passed as my girlfriend
because I like you.

17:00.936 --> 17:02.312
I SAID YOU PASSED AS MY GIRLFRIEND
BECAUSE I LIKE YOU

17:03.563 --> 17:06.107
And I told you that you could use me
because I like you.

17:06.733 --> 17:11.071
Maybe I'll catch feelings for someone
if I go on a few more dates.

17:11.363 --> 17:13.823
They're all nice guys.

17:14.533 --> 17:16.284
You'll give them that many chances?

17:16.409 --> 17:18.870
If they're that nice,
don't waste their time.

17:18.954 --> 17:20.997
Let them go so that they can find the one.

17:21.248 --> 17:23.833
If you're not interested in someone,
turn them down properly.

17:23.917 --> 17:26.127
That's also a part of being respectful
in dating.

17:33.593 --> 17:34.886
I'm sorry.

17:34.970 --> 17:37.138
I don't think we'd be a good match.

17:37.264 --> 17:39.015
I hope you find someone great.

17:42.352 --> 17:43.728
YOU WANT TO WATCH A MOVIE TONIGHT?

17:45.146 --> 17:47.274
Your mother is so charismatic.

17:47.357 --> 17:50.485
I can be your umbrella when you're out.

17:50.569 --> 17:52.237
But you don't need one. It's too sunny.

17:52.320 --> 17:54.030
I guess this is it for us.

17:54.114 --> 17:56.783
The end

17:56.866 --> 17:59.953
Know that they can reject you
just as much as you can reject them.

18:00.203 --> 18:02.122
That's how blind dates work.

18:02.622 --> 18:03.665
Yeah.

18:06.126 --> 18:07.127
Right.

18:22.350 --> 18:24.269
- Hello.
- Hello.

18:24.936 --> 18:26.354
How are you?

18:26.688 --> 18:28.273
Don't fight.

18:29.065 --> 18:30.984
Seoltang!

18:31.234 --> 18:32.235
Hello.

18:32.986 --> 18:35.322
Thanks for coming on such short notice.

18:35.864 --> 18:39.951
Seoltang, you're sparkling clean!
You look wonderful.

18:40.243 --> 18:43.955
Ask your new owner
for all the pets in the world, okay?

18:46.249 --> 18:47.709
Okay, thank you.

18:51.880 --> 18:54.299
80, GEUMYEONGHWA 22-GIL,
PAJU, GYEONGGI-DO

18:55.091 --> 18:56.593
I don't want to adopt him anymore.

18:56.885 --> 18:57.886
Why?

18:58.303 --> 19:00.805
I'm sure
that wasn't an overnight decision.

19:00.889 --> 19:02.223
I liked him in the photos

19:02.307 --> 19:05.310
because he reminded me
of the dog I had as a kid.

19:05.393 --> 19:07.520
But he's too different in person.

19:07.604 --> 19:09.522
He's too big and too hairy.

19:09.689 --> 19:12.192
Maybe it's because he's a stray.
What if he has diseases?

19:12.275 --> 19:13.902
Please watch your mouth.

19:13.985 --> 19:16.738
It's not like animals understand humans.

19:17.155 --> 19:19.824
Animals can feel everything, too.

19:19.908 --> 19:23.286
They can tell how we feel
based on our faces and voices.

19:23.370 --> 19:25.455
They know it when you don't like them.

19:25.747 --> 19:30.293
I hope you'll experience
what Seoltang just experienced one day.

19:30.377 --> 19:33.046
I don't think you'll get it
until you experience it yourself.

19:33.129 --> 19:34.172
Excuse me?

19:34.339 --> 19:35.340
Let's go, Seoltang.

19:35.632 --> 19:36.841
Excuse me? Let go.

19:36.925 --> 19:38.426
- Let's go.
- Excuse me?

19:38.510 --> 19:39.511
Say that again.

19:47.102 --> 19:48.103
POLICE WITHOUT CORRUPTION

19:48.186 --> 19:49.562
Oh, gosh, where?

19:50.230 --> 19:51.272
This way?

19:51.356 --> 19:53.066
Oh, goodness.

19:54.901 --> 19:56.736
- No running.
- Yes, sir.

19:58.571 --> 20:00.407
He tried to scam us!

20:00.490 --> 20:01.533
Hey!

20:02.534 --> 20:04.953
Mr. Song! Are you okay?

20:05.286 --> 20:06.746
Who the hell do you think you are?

20:07.038 --> 20:10.625
You think dogs are toys?
Come on, you should know better!

20:10.792 --> 20:13.378
You need to think it through
before adopting a pet!

20:13.461 --> 20:14.754
And be responsible!

20:14.838 --> 20:16.339
What the hell are you saying?

20:16.423 --> 20:17.549
What did you say?

20:17.632 --> 20:20.260
Gosh, even dogs are better than you are.

20:20.343 --> 20:21.344
Come here.

20:21.428 --> 20:24.180
- Are you okay, my Seoltang?
- Who the hell are you?

20:24.973 --> 20:26.558
What do you think you're doing?

20:26.641 --> 20:28.143
- Are you okay?
- Hey!

20:28.226 --> 20:30.854
- Did you just push me?
- So what?

20:31.271 --> 20:33.314
Stop pissing me off.

20:34.441 --> 20:35.942
- Say it again. What?
- Please.

20:36.025 --> 20:37.736
- Stop.
- What was it?

20:37.819 --> 20:39.529
- Stop it!
- Sir!

20:39.612 --> 20:41.990
- What the hell are you doing?
- Hey!

20:49.205 --> 20:53.001
PAJU SEOBU POLICE STATION

20:53.752 --> 20:56.337
I didn't think you'd call me
to the police station.

20:56.421 --> 21:00.008
I thought you'd handle it
more like a grown-up.

21:06.389 --> 21:09.017
We had good teamwork, though.

21:09.184 --> 21:12.937
I thought you were gentle.
You're quite a fighter.

21:13.021 --> 21:14.397
You know how to hold a grudge.

21:14.481 --> 21:18.359
I lost it when he gave up Seoltang
five minutes after meeting him.

21:18.443 --> 21:20.361
That's terrible.

21:20.445 --> 21:24.866
Can people stop setting such record?
It's nothing to be proud of.

21:24.949 --> 21:25.992
I know.

21:26.367 --> 21:28.036
Oh, no, that's not good.

21:28.286 --> 21:29.788
You're allergic to dogs.

21:29.871 --> 21:33.416
I can keep him
and return him to the shelter on Monday.

21:33.500 --> 21:36.085
No, I'll take him.
I'll be fine with my meds for a few days.

21:36.169 --> 21:37.545
If that's what you want.

21:37.629 --> 21:39.005
Seoltang

21:39.631 --> 21:42.342
I guess
an even better home is waiting for you.

21:46.679 --> 21:48.807
It's mine.

21:48.890 --> 21:49.891
Oh.

21:53.978 --> 21:56.356
Mr. Eun, I heard my friend booked
the wedding hall.

21:56.439 --> 21:57.857
Thanks for coming on your day off

21:57.941 --> 22:00.068
I'm touched once again.

22:00.151 --> 22:02.111
Sure. Smiley face.

22:03.488 --> 22:05.198
Are you waiting for someone to text you?

22:05.281 --> 22:07.075
Yeah, Ui-yeong.

22:11.079 --> 22:12.372
Oh.

22:14.082 --> 22:16.876
I was the matchmaker

22:16.960 --> 22:19.087
so I should be honest and tell you.

22:19.587 --> 22:21.005
Ui-yeong...

22:21.089 --> 22:23.550
I know she went on another blind date.
I saw her.

22:25.552 --> 22:26.886
You saw her?

22:27.178 --> 22:28.471
And you're still waiting?

22:29.556 --> 22:33.810
She said she'd text me,
and it's not exactly over yet.

22:34.394 --> 22:38.022
I can't tell if you're confident
or just stupid.

22:39.732 --> 22:42.861
I'll know for sure
if I just see her one more time.

22:46.865 --> 22:49.993
Man, that's tricky.

22:50.285 --> 22:53.788
I'm a matchmaker, not Cupid.

22:57.458 --> 23:01.337
Run into her one more time, then.

23:01.880 --> 23:04.465
Sorry? What do you mean?

23:04.549 --> 23:07.343
I'll fix it for you.

23:07.594 --> 23:09.596
It's a small world at the hotel.

23:09.679 --> 23:11.389
It's a workplace to some

23:11.472 --> 23:14.434
where they have to stay all day every day.

23:14.809 --> 23:17.353
And to others,
it's a place for business meetings

23:17.604 --> 23:20.565
or a nice place to have coffee
with their friends.

23:21.107 --> 23:23.610
So, just run into her at the hotel.

23:25.028 --> 23:26.571
Oh.

23:30.199 --> 23:31.534
"Hey, Ui-yeong!"

23:32.035 --> 23:33.912
"Is this the hotel you work at?"

23:34.871 --> 23:37.540
"Wow, I see."

23:37.957 --> 23:40.710
"I'm here to meet a friend."

23:44.047 --> 23:46.758
"What a coincidence."

23:46.841 --> 23:48.843
"Would you like to grab lunch together?"

23:50.219 --> 23:52.180
Why would I shake her hand?

23:54.307 --> 23:55.433
Ui-yeong...

23:56.684 --> 23:58.895
"Ui-yeong."

24:00.563 --> 24:02.148
Seoltang...

24:03.149 --> 24:04.359
What do I do?

24:06.027 --> 24:07.195
It's called "HOME."

24:07.278 --> 24:11.240
It's quite popular among people
interested in home renovations.

24:11.324 --> 24:12.784
COMPANY PORTFOLIO FOR HOME

24:13.493 --> 24:16.663
They also do renovations for cafés.

24:16.788 --> 24:18.665
We're not dilly-dallying.

24:18.748 --> 24:21.334
Let's just stick with Homage.
We work with them all the time.

24:22.001 --> 24:24.712
I know Homage is great,
but so is this place.

24:24.837 --> 24:28.549
Why don't we choose between the two
after they submit their proposals?

24:28.925 --> 24:32.387
That's extra work for us.
Is that necessary?

24:32.470 --> 24:35.223
An important part of our jobs is
to create a great space.

24:35.306 --> 24:36.641
Let's ask for a proposal.

24:36.724 --> 24:38.184
Why don't we give them two weeks?

24:38.309 --> 24:40.561
Just give them a week
and say it can be a rough draft.

24:40.645 --> 24:44.148
A week sounds too short.

24:44.232 --> 24:46.442
Let's do ten days, then.

24:46.526 --> 24:50.113
Why even ask me
if you'll just do whatever you want?

24:50.405 --> 24:53.783
I'll call Homage.
You can take care of the rest, then.

24:53.866 --> 24:55.910
Okay, I'll contact HOME.

24:55.994 --> 24:57.161
No, Sae-byeok will.

24:57.286 --> 25:00.665
Why don't we ask her to contact them
since she found them?

25:00.748 --> 25:02.375
I'll send the e-mail.

25:02.458 --> 25:04.210
Let's leave her to set the details.

25:05.920 --> 25:07.213
Are you up for it?

25:07.672 --> 25:09.799
Yes, I'll do it.

25:11.259 --> 25:13.803
PROPOSAL FOR THE HILLS SEOUL'S COLLAB
WITH DEERFIDDICH

25:13.886 --> 25:14.887
YOUR MAIL HAS BEEN SENT

25:14.971 --> 25:15.972
All done.

25:16.055 --> 25:17.098
- Sae-byeok.
- Yes?

25:17.181 --> 25:20.018
I e-mailed them.
You can call them and go home.

25:20.226 --> 25:21.310
Okay.

25:21.394 --> 25:23.104
- Good work today.
- See you tomorrow.

25:23.187 --> 25:24.731
- Go home soon, okay?
- Okay!

25:38.870 --> 25:40.580
Hello, this is Lee Eun-ho from HOME.

25:40.872 --> 25:42.081
Hello.

25:42.165 --> 25:44.959
I'm Sim Sae-byeok from Purchasing
at The Hills Seoul.

25:45.043 --> 25:47.545
We just sent you an e-mail.

25:49.672 --> 25:50.840
Oh.

25:51.632 --> 25:53.676
- It's a pop-up store?
- That's right.

25:54.177 --> 25:56.512
HOME WILL CHECK THE E-MAIL AND LET US KNOW

26:04.896 --> 26:06.439
She's the intern.

26:06.522 --> 26:08.316
- Who?
- You know, with Do-hyun.

26:08.649 --> 26:10.443
- That's the intern?
- Yeah!

26:12.403 --> 26:14.614
Is work just a playground for people
these days?

26:14.697 --> 26:15.823
Tell me about it.

26:27.376 --> 26:31.005
Mr. Kang, can I talk to you for a sec?

26:36.803 --> 26:38.638
No, I'll bring it.

26:41.891 --> 26:43.893
Thank you. Enjoy your drink.

26:43.976 --> 26:44.977
Thank you.

26:56.572 --> 26:58.866
Did you think about it?

26:59.617 --> 27:00.618
Yes.

27:02.537 --> 27:05.915
I don't want to make things awkward
with Ui-yeong

27:06.582 --> 27:09.627
and I need to focus
on finding a job right now.

27:10.753 --> 27:12.004
I'm sorry.

27:16.092 --> 27:18.719
I've been rejected for a similar reason.

27:19.220 --> 27:21.514
I backed down then because I was a nobody

27:22.682 --> 27:24.100
but things are different now.

27:24.308 --> 27:26.102
I can pay for all our meals

27:26.185 --> 27:28.646
and support you until you land a job.

27:28.813 --> 27:30.690
Think about what works best for you.

27:30.773 --> 27:33.651
To be honest, you just made it harder
for me to get a job.

27:33.734 --> 27:35.903
I haven't even proved myself yet

27:35.987 --> 27:39.824
and people at the hotel already know me
because of you.

27:40.616 --> 27:43.911
I want to do really well on this project.

27:44.662 --> 27:47.081
Please let me focus on work.

27:49.208 --> 27:52.086
Please excuse me, then.

28:16.652 --> 28:18.613
Do we need more frame structure
for the legs?

28:19.363 --> 28:21.949
We're going to use ropes
and minimize using frames.

28:23.242 --> 28:25.244
Eun-ho, did you see the e-mail?

28:25.703 --> 28:27.330
- Which one?
- The pop-up at The Hills.

28:27.413 --> 28:29.665
Yeah, but I'm going to turn it down.

28:29.749 --> 28:31.250
We're too busy already.

28:31.334 --> 28:33.711
You don't even like
these temporary projects.

28:33.794 --> 28:35.338
That's true.

28:36.839 --> 28:38.299
But we need to take this.

28:39.425 --> 28:42.136
What are you talking about?
We have enough work already.

28:42.220 --> 28:44.472
No, I want to do this.

28:44.555 --> 28:46.599
Huh? Where are you going?

28:46.933 --> 28:48.517
To check out the space at the hotel.

28:48.684 --> 28:50.728
Right now? Huh?

28:51.103 --> 28:52.897
- Are you really doing it?
- Yeah.

28:53.189 --> 28:55.316
I was going to go, anyway.

28:57.151 --> 28:58.945
- Ui-yeong.
- Yeah?

28:59.612 --> 29:02.698
I got a reply from Mr. Lee at HOME.

29:02.782 --> 29:04.325
He wants to participate in the bid.

29:04.408 --> 29:06.285
Really? That's great!

29:06.494 --> 29:10.081
Sorry about leaving you and Hyun-min
to do all the work.

29:10.164 --> 29:12.458
I'll buy you a nice meal soon.

29:27.348 --> 29:28.766
So, this is it.

29:30.059 --> 29:31.060
Oh?

29:34.689 --> 29:36.315
- I'm so sorry.
- Are you okay?

29:36.899 --> 29:37.900
I'm okay, thank you.

29:49.495 --> 29:51.038
I'm sure I'll see her again.

29:56.002 --> 29:58.004
- I'll go after I take this call.
- Okay.

30:01.382 --> 30:02.383
Hello?

30:02.466 --> 30:03.884
Is this Ms. Lee Ui-yeong?

30:04.051 --> 30:06.846
I'm Kim Su-on. Eun-mi gave me your number.

30:07.013 --> 30:09.932
Oh, I see. Hello.

30:10.349 --> 30:12.268
Sorry about calling you out of the blue.

30:12.435 --> 30:14.603
Are you free tomorrow evening?

30:19.567 --> 30:21.235
Eun-mi's told me so much about you.

30:21.319 --> 30:23.112
She said you were such a nice person

30:23.195 --> 30:25.281
so I wasn't expecting
such a beautiful woman.

30:26.991 --> 30:28.326
But you're beautiful.

30:28.951 --> 30:32.163
KIM SU-ON, 35, RUNS A FAMILY BUSINESS

30:32.246 --> 30:33.873
Oh, thank you.

30:35.207 --> 30:39.045
I heard you were friends with Ho-jin
for a long time.

30:39.128 --> 30:40.129
Oh, that bastard...

30:41.047 --> 30:43.090
I've been friends with him for 20 years.

30:43.799 --> 30:47.053
We should go on a double date one day.

30:53.517 --> 30:55.811
So, what do your parents like to do?

30:56.520 --> 30:58.856
My parents? Not me?

30:58.939 --> 30:59.940
Yeah.

31:00.524 --> 31:01.650
Oh...

31:01.817 --> 31:05.321
My mom's been doing yoga
for a very long time.

31:05.780 --> 31:09.825
My dad used to love fishing and camping
back in the day

31:10.242 --> 31:11.577
but not anymore.

31:11.660 --> 31:14.205
I heard your father works
for the railroad.

31:16.082 --> 31:17.750
Yeah, he does.

31:17.833 --> 31:19.960
And you don't live with him
because of his work.

31:22.421 --> 31:24.715
It's not just because of his work.

31:25.383 --> 31:28.344
I don't know the whole story
because it's between my parents

31:28.761 --> 31:32.640
but their personalities and values were
too different.

31:32.848 --> 31:35.017
They've been living separately
since I was a kid.

31:35.309 --> 31:36.310
I see.

31:36.811 --> 31:38.687
So, are they divorced?

31:39.271 --> 31:41.482
No, they just live separately.

31:41.565 --> 31:42.608
I see.

31:43.651 --> 31:45.778
I'm so glad.

31:46.237 --> 31:47.238
"Glad"?

31:47.321 --> 31:49.407
You seem like you were raised
in a loving family.

31:49.824 --> 31:52.535
I wouldn't have known that wasn't the case
if you didn't tell me.

32:22.356 --> 32:23.607
Hey, Eun-mi.

32:23.899 --> 32:25.526
I heard you had dinner with Su-on.

32:25.609 --> 32:27.486
How did it go? Isn't he so funny?

32:29.447 --> 32:31.907
He did say a lot of not-so-funny things
with confidence.

32:31.991 --> 32:33.742
He's just honest.

32:34.076 --> 32:35.327
He told me

32:35.411 --> 32:38.289
he's only interested in flawless women

32:38.372 --> 32:39.832
but wants to see you again.

32:43.502 --> 32:44.795
What does he mean by that?

32:45.045 --> 32:47.756
Oh, I didn't know
your parents didn't live together.

32:48.090 --> 32:50.301
Why didn't you tell me?
I thought we were friends.

32:50.551 --> 32:52.052
I never tried to hide it from you.

32:52.386 --> 32:54.555
It's not like I have to tell that
to all my friends.

32:54.722 --> 32:58.392
The point is, things worked out,
and he wants to see you again.

32:58.476 --> 33:02.188
Oh, he wants to know
if your parents have a retirement fund.

33:02.980 --> 33:04.023
What?

33:04.857 --> 33:06.150
Why does he need to know that?

33:06.484 --> 33:08.360
It's good for you to ask him, too.

33:08.444 --> 33:11.572
It doesn't have to be in detail.
Just ask him if they're financially okay.

33:13.324 --> 33:15.159
What a ridiculous question.

33:15.576 --> 33:16.577
Bye.

34:28.148 --> 34:29.567
DAD

34:33.988 --> 34:37.199
I can't call him out of nowhere
just to ask him that.

34:43.581 --> 34:44.623
Hey, Mom.

34:45.958 --> 34:47.876
- What are you doing?
- Nothing much.

34:50.588 --> 34:52.339
Don't be on your phone all night.

34:52.423 --> 34:54.425
I'm not in high school anymore.

34:54.508 --> 34:55.509
Whatever.

35:03.976 --> 35:05.811
Yeah, that's pushing it.

35:06.353 --> 35:07.688
My parents' retirement?

35:07.771 --> 35:10.149
Guys didn't need to know that to date me
in the past.

35:14.903 --> 35:17.948
I don't think Su-on and I are compatible.

35:18.449 --> 35:20.034
Please tell him that.

35:26.498 --> 35:27.583
Alright.

35:28.542 --> 35:30.502
Huh? What?

35:33.005 --> 35:34.340
I forgot to take the tag off!

35:34.798 --> 35:36.508
Time for me to return it.

35:39.762 --> 35:41.805
This is a lot. What do we do?

35:42.056 --> 35:43.182
It's all due this week.

35:43.265 --> 35:44.600
- What?
- This week.

36:13.212 --> 36:15.547
You know how we're getting proposals
from the companies?

36:15.631 --> 36:17.591
Let's just get one from Homage.

36:17.675 --> 36:19.176
Sorry? Why?

36:19.259 --> 36:21.720
Why bother with the others?
That's a waste of time.

36:21.887 --> 36:24.056
We could've just gone with Homage
from the start.

36:24.139 --> 36:27.101
We're just asking one more company
so you have more work.

36:27.184 --> 36:28.936
Let's keep things simple.

36:29.186 --> 36:32.815
I'll ask Ui-yeong about it.

36:32.898 --> 36:36.860
Are you saying you need her permission
for what I just said?

36:38.070 --> 36:40.030
No, that's not what I mean.

36:40.906 --> 36:42.074
I'm sorry.

36:44.618 --> 36:45.911
- Sae-byeok.
- Yes?

36:45.994 --> 36:48.789
It takes competence
to handle a situation like this.

36:49.039 --> 36:53.168
I'll make sure Homage prepares
the perfect proposal.

36:53.252 --> 36:55.963
Your job is to tell HOME
that we don't need their proposal.

36:56.046 --> 36:57.214
Okay, noted.

37:08.308 --> 37:09.685
- Hello.
- Hello.

37:09.768 --> 37:11.603
CONFERENCE ROOM

37:11.687 --> 37:13.188
I'm Oh Man-joong, the CEO of Homage.

37:13.272 --> 37:15.858
I love your business card.

37:20.362 --> 37:23.782
I set up a successful exhibition
at The Place Hotel this year

37:23.866 --> 37:25.951
and what was the project
that ended last week?

37:26.660 --> 37:28.829
Oh, the Bella Art Gallery.

37:29.371 --> 37:33.625
As mentioned in the e-mail,
our exhibition is focused on the objet.

37:33.709 --> 37:35.335
We'll make some display cases, then.

37:35.544 --> 37:39.047
Show them the jewelry shop we opened
at the New World Department Store in 2017.

37:39.131 --> 37:40.716
- Show them the design.
- Yes, sir.

37:48.974 --> 37:50.559
Oh, this shop.

37:53.645 --> 37:55.314
We have to talk about the deadline.

37:55.397 --> 37:56.982
We'd like the store to be ready...

37:57.065 --> 37:59.443
We're not running a corner shop here.

37:59.526 --> 38:01.612
We've done hundreds of pop-ups.

38:01.737 --> 38:05.073
We work with city halls, malls,
and art galleries.

38:05.157 --> 38:06.784
You think we'd miss a deadline?

38:07.034 --> 38:09.661
I'm sure you wouldn't,
but we still need to confirm it...

38:09.745 --> 38:11.747
Sara, show them the proposal.

38:11.830 --> 38:12.831
Yes, sir.

38:16.543 --> 38:18.796
You have it already?

38:22.007 --> 38:23.133
My gosh.

38:27.346 --> 38:31.016
That's a lot of detail
in such a short period.

38:31.099 --> 38:33.268
We'll use Lauan plywood

38:33.560 --> 38:36.021
to highlight the vintage vibe
of the whiskey.

38:36.104 --> 38:38.690
We'll finish some parts with Formica

38:38.774 --> 38:41.527
to add Deerfiddich's signature color
to the wood.

38:42.361 --> 38:44.238
You got it done so well in no time!

38:44.905 --> 38:46.657
You're a pro, indeed.

38:47.741 --> 38:48.992
What do you think?

38:49.076 --> 38:51.787
What? Oh, it's great.

38:58.377 --> 39:00.629
It looks very classy.

39:01.171 --> 39:02.798
- Great work.
- Good job.

39:02.881 --> 39:04.591
- See you.
- This way.

39:05.092 --> 39:07.553
Thanks so much, sir.

39:07.636 --> 39:09.721
- Bye.
- I love your outfit today, too.

39:09.805 --> 39:12.391
Do you have time after this?

39:12.808 --> 39:15.143
How about a drink together?

39:19.106 --> 39:20.482
Oh, Sae-byeok

39:20.566 --> 39:23.819
have you not scheduled a meeting
with HOME's CEO yet?

39:25.654 --> 39:27.656
Oh, well, that's...

39:28.073 --> 39:30.284
The CEO called

39:32.119 --> 39:33.620
and he...

39:34.413 --> 39:36.164
Something's going on at HOME

39:36.707 --> 39:38.750
so he doesn't have time.

39:40.127 --> 39:41.753
He said he needed to drop our project.

39:41.837 --> 39:42.838
Drop it?

39:43.130 --> 39:46.049
Didn't he agree on the project
a while ago?

39:51.179 --> 39:53.515
That's why you seem so down.

39:53.765 --> 39:56.184
You must be so disappointed.
You worked so hard for it.

39:56.393 --> 39:58.687
It's okay. This happens from time to time.

39:59.229 --> 40:00.272
Okay.

40:00.606 --> 40:04.192
I'm glad we found talented people
to work with.

40:04.276 --> 40:06.028
That's a huge relief.

40:07.195 --> 40:08.280
It's okay, Sae-byeok.

40:08.614 --> 40:09.948
- Okay.
- Yeah.

40:14.828 --> 40:16.496
- Let's clean up.
- Okay.

40:27.716 --> 40:29.885
Is this layout too complicated?

40:30.844 --> 40:33.055
That looks nice!

40:34.056 --> 40:35.265
It's perfect

40:37.309 --> 40:38.435
but we're out.

40:39.645 --> 40:40.687
What?

40:41.772 --> 40:44.107
What do you mean?
We haven't even had a meeting.

40:45.817 --> 40:47.361
You got a cigarette?

40:47.527 --> 40:48.695
I quit ages ago.

40:50.656 --> 40:53.659
I hate how they just said
it was an internal decision.

40:53.742 --> 40:56.703
They could've at least said
we were over their budget!

40:56.870 --> 40:58.872
This is just plain disrespectful!

40:58.956 --> 41:01.333
I bet they already decided on a company
before asking us.

41:01.625 --> 41:04.044
Do they think it's our first time
getting dropped?

41:04.544 --> 41:08.882
If that's really the case,
it's good that it ended here.

41:10.092 --> 41:12.928
Didn't you pull multiple all-nighters
for the project?

41:13.512 --> 41:15.639
You want to get some fresh air somewhere?

41:16.264 --> 41:18.767
Sure, let's take Sua.

41:26.358 --> 41:28.151
- See you tomorrow.
- See you.

41:29.945 --> 41:30.988
Hello?

41:31.279 --> 41:33.615
I guess you didn't save my number.

41:33.699 --> 41:35.117
I'm Su-on.

41:35.784 --> 41:38.537
I told Eun-mi I wanted to see you again.

41:38.954 --> 41:41.498
Did Eun-mi not tell him what I said?

41:41.707 --> 41:43.000
Do you have time after work?

41:43.333 --> 41:46.294
I'm near your hotel right now
for something else.

41:46.753 --> 41:48.088
Oh, are you?

41:49.548 --> 41:51.425
Sure, I have time.

41:53.552 --> 41:54.594
Okay.

42:05.856 --> 42:07.566
I brought it to return it, though.

42:17.200 --> 42:20.454
You look great in that dress, too.

42:21.788 --> 42:23.623
It's hard to look so good in pink.

42:25.292 --> 42:26.501
Thank you.

42:27.627 --> 42:29.296
Su-on

42:29.629 --> 42:33.050
I heard you had questions
about my parents' retirement plans.

42:33.842 --> 42:35.469
Yeah, why?

42:37.179 --> 42:41.683
It's not like we're seeing each other now
to get married.

42:41.975 --> 42:46.063
With that said, their retirement plans are
between me and my parents.

42:46.480 --> 42:49.733
It's not for you to know about
or prepare for.

42:50.859 --> 42:51.943
Oh, right.

42:52.903 --> 42:54.029
I get what you mean.

42:54.654 --> 42:56.406
It's okay. Just forget what I said.

42:59.785 --> 43:02.746
Let's lighten the mood.
Should we order some wine?

43:03.246 --> 43:04.289
Sure.

43:05.457 --> 43:07.125
- Excuse me.
- Yes.

43:10.962 --> 43:13.381
We'll get a cheese platter

43:15.759 --> 43:16.843
with this wine.

43:17.636 --> 43:18.720
Jeong-u?

43:18.845 --> 43:20.180
I'll get that ready for you.

43:36.905 --> 43:38.323
SHIN JI-SU

43:38.949 --> 43:40.075
Oh, right.

43:40.158 --> 43:42.452
Jeong-u had a tattoo on his neck.

43:59.970 --> 44:01.847
I heard you could drink quite a bit.

44:01.930 --> 44:03.557
How much can you drink, exactly?

44:04.391 --> 44:07.686
It depends on the drink,
but I can handle a bottle of wine.

44:07.853 --> 44:09.563
That's a lot more than me.

44:09.980 --> 44:12.440
I should pour some more for you, then.

44:14.568 --> 44:17.821
Please excuse me.
I need to use the bathroom.

44:17.946 --> 44:18.947
Okay.

44:26.872 --> 44:28.206
Excuse me.

44:29.541 --> 44:33.295
Maybe this question is a bit random

44:33.503 --> 44:36.756
but do you have a twin brother?

44:37.465 --> 44:39.342
No, I don't.

44:39.759 --> 44:42.012
Oh, sorry about that.

44:44.139 --> 44:45.348
My last name is different

44:46.099 --> 44:47.976
from the guy you think is my twin, right?

44:48.727 --> 44:49.728
Sorry?

44:49.978 --> 44:52.647
My last name is Shin, and his is Lee.

44:54.191 --> 44:55.525
Oh, that's true...

44:58.612 --> 44:59.696
It's you, right?

45:00.530 --> 45:01.531
You're Jeong-u.

45:02.032 --> 45:03.116
What are you doing here?

45:03.241 --> 45:05.285
Can't you tell? I work here.

45:05.368 --> 45:06.494
Yeah, why here?

45:08.163 --> 45:09.289
Are you on another date?

45:10.415 --> 45:13.251
- You're really desperate.
- What?

45:13.335 --> 45:15.962
You also couldn't stop talking
about finding a guy then.

45:19.090 --> 45:20.842
He's not so bad.

45:20.926 --> 45:23.970
He has eyes, a nose, and lips.

45:24.054 --> 45:25.513
He's decently dressed.

45:25.931 --> 45:27.098
That's what you're into.

45:27.891 --> 45:29.267
What am I into?

45:29.351 --> 45:30.560
Good luck.

45:30.727 --> 45:33.271
If you don't like him

45:34.356 --> 45:36.066
do this.

45:36.566 --> 45:38.235
That's your sign, okay?

45:38.944 --> 45:39.986
Got it?

45:40.487 --> 45:41.529
Hey...

45:43.657 --> 45:44.783
Man!

45:46.326 --> 45:47.744
What was that about?

46:04.761 --> 46:07.013
Hey, Su-on

46:07.305 --> 46:10.308
why don't we go
somewhere more comfortable?

46:13.103 --> 46:15.647
Sure, do you know a place?

46:15.772 --> 46:17.732
Not really.

46:18.024 --> 46:20.443
But anywhere would be better than here.

46:20.860 --> 46:23.321
Oh, okay.

46:24.281 --> 46:27.158
Sure, then.
I'll just quickly use the bathroom.

46:27.325 --> 46:28.326
Okay.

46:41.298 --> 46:43.049
Seriously, what is he doing here?

46:43.300 --> 46:44.718
Hey, Eun-mi told me

46:45.176 --> 46:46.928
Ui-yeong didn't want a second date.

46:49.180 --> 46:51.808
How dare she reject me? She's a nobody.

46:52.392 --> 46:54.185
I got bored, so I asked her out again.

46:55.020 --> 46:56.521
But you know what's hilarious?

46:57.564 --> 46:59.524
She didn't even take
the tag off her dress.

47:00.692 --> 47:03.778
Do I get to keep her if I take it off?

47:06.197 --> 47:07.449
Seriously.

47:09.576 --> 47:10.577
Yeah.

47:11.828 --> 47:13.830
No idea.
She wants to go somewhere comfortable.

47:14.831 --> 47:16.875
Where should I take her? A motel?

47:19.294 --> 47:20.962
Oh, it's so slippery.

47:21.379 --> 47:23.256
Sorry about that.

47:27.177 --> 47:28.261
Hey...

47:30.263 --> 47:33.308
But the floor is dry.

47:37.479 --> 47:38.563
- Let's get out.
- Huh?

47:38.646 --> 47:40.273
- What?
- I'll tell you outside.

47:40.357 --> 47:41.983
- Let go.
- What's going on?

47:43.068 --> 47:45.153
Su-on, he's...

47:45.236 --> 47:46.321
Ui-yeong.

47:46.488 --> 47:48.281
I guess your taste in men has changed.

47:49.032 --> 47:52.285
You pushed me in the bathroom
on purpose, didn't you?

47:52.369 --> 47:53.620
Do you know him?

47:53.828 --> 47:55.872
No, I don't. Let's just leave.

47:55.955 --> 47:57.248
Are you really going to leave?

47:58.083 --> 48:00.293
I know how you really feel.

48:00.627 --> 48:02.670
You came here because you missed me.

48:03.129 --> 48:04.506
What the hell are you doing?

48:04.589 --> 48:07.175
I couldn't even sleep or eat
because I missed you.

48:07.258 --> 48:09.344
Look at me. Don't I look thinner?

48:09.803 --> 48:10.804
Hey!

48:10.887 --> 48:13.932
Oh, so, she used me.

48:14.224 --> 48:17.018
- What?
- What a damn shitty day.

48:17.560 --> 48:19.312
You acted all classy

48:19.396 --> 48:20.980
so I didn't know you were a whore.

48:21.147 --> 48:22.899
You know who the real whore is?

48:22.982 --> 48:25.193
- Did you just push me?
- Stop.

48:25.402 --> 48:26.653
- Stop.
- Damn it.

48:26.736 --> 48:28.196
- Stop it.
- Hey!

48:29.531 --> 48:30.657
Are you okay?

48:30.740 --> 48:32.283
- What's going on?
- Is he okay?

48:32.617 --> 48:33.618
Are you hurt?

48:33.701 --> 48:35.662
You pushed me first.

48:38.164 --> 48:39.332
You're kidding me.

48:41.167 --> 48:42.502
I'm sorry.

48:56.641 --> 48:57.725
I'll take you home.

48:58.893 --> 49:00.395
Why would you?

49:01.813 --> 49:02.981
You had wine.

49:03.940 --> 49:06.192
You want to be nice to me
after ruining my date?

49:06.276 --> 49:07.777
Just pick a side.

49:08.111 --> 49:09.529
Did I do something wrong?

49:10.155 --> 49:11.948
Tell me. Let me try to understand you.

49:13.408 --> 49:14.451
Well...

49:17.036 --> 49:20.206
You put your hands on your ears.
I thought that was a signal.

49:20.331 --> 49:21.708
Asking for my help.

49:26.838 --> 49:28.882
I'm a joke to you, aren't I?

49:28.965 --> 49:30.216
You think I'm ridiculous.

49:30.467 --> 49:32.010
And that I'm too desperate for love.

49:32.218 --> 49:33.303
It's not like that.

49:33.887 --> 49:36.306
But you know,
I think you're more ridiculous.

49:36.764 --> 49:38.683
You're so ridiculous
that it's not even funny.

49:41.394 --> 49:42.687
You're a lie.

49:43.480 --> 49:45.857
You lied that whole night,
and even your name is a lie.

49:46.858 --> 49:50.236
And you think I'm ridiculous?
That's hilarious to me.

50:37.867 --> 50:39.661
When are you going to stop following me?

50:39.869 --> 50:41.246
Until you're not mad anymore.

50:42.580 --> 50:43.581
What is he saying?

50:45.416 --> 50:46.543
You can go now.

50:53.091 --> 50:54.634
THE SEAGULL

50:54.717 --> 50:55.760
Here.

50:56.386 --> 50:57.387
What's this?

50:58.179 --> 51:00.473
I'm not Lee Jeong-u. I'm Shin Ji-su.

51:01.558 --> 51:04.561
I'm an actor, and I'm 29.

51:06.187 --> 51:09.482
I had to go on that blind date
for someone.

51:12.318 --> 51:13.570
I can't tell you why.

51:15.113 --> 51:16.739
I don't care about your reasons.

51:17.240 --> 51:19.033
That makes no difference to me.

51:22.078 --> 51:23.121
Just take it.

51:24.247 --> 51:25.873
This is like my ID.

51:26.416 --> 51:29.002
I don't want everything about me
to be a lie to you.

51:33.464 --> 51:34.674
THE SEAGULL

51:34.757 --> 51:36.092
I don't understand you.

51:37.010 --> 51:39.804
I don't understand
why you're so desperate to find love.

51:40.555 --> 51:43.391
But I never thought you were ridiculous.

51:49.564 --> 51:51.274
Okay, you can go.

51:52.150 --> 51:53.151
Wait.

52:14.881 --> 52:17.133
What was that just now?

52:17.592 --> 52:21.220
You had something in the back.

52:26.768 --> 52:28.311
Come to the show.

52:30.521 --> 52:31.564
Bye, then.

53:05.306 --> 53:07.892
THE SEAGULL

53:22.990 --> 53:25.743
- Hello?
- Why is it so hard to reach you?

53:26.744 --> 53:27.829
Are you out?

53:31.040 --> 53:32.166
You okay?

53:32.875 --> 53:35.837
I even canceled my class
because you sounded so glum.

53:36.087 --> 53:37.422
No, I'm not okay.

53:38.631 --> 53:41.884
Two men fought because of me.
It was a total mess.

53:42.927 --> 53:44.512
It was terrifying.

53:45.722 --> 53:48.099
How can that happen on a blind date?

53:48.558 --> 53:50.893
You're still pale from panicking.

53:50.977 --> 53:53.730
I told you you'd get a heartburn
if you went too fast.

53:53.980 --> 53:55.606
You need to rest

53:55.690 --> 53:57.650
- after working out...
- Seung-jun said

53:57.900 --> 53:59.944
our bodies needed rest

54:00.027 --> 54:01.529
after overworking them.

54:01.612 --> 54:02.822
You need a break first!

54:02.905 --> 54:05.491
He said that was how you avoided injuries.

54:06.075 --> 54:08.244
And he said the same went for our hearts.

54:08.327 --> 54:10.204
What's the point of telling you, anyway?

54:21.549 --> 54:23.593
LEE HYUN-JU:
ARE YOU STILL INTERESTED IN A BLIND DATE?

54:27.054 --> 54:30.641
So, I decided to take a break
from blind dates.

54:30.892 --> 54:32.435
But I wasn't giving up.

54:32.769 --> 54:36.063
It was a little break
for a stronger takeoff in the future.

54:38.649 --> 54:41.110
Let's go home, girls.

54:41.819 --> 54:42.945
- What?
- Huh?

54:43.029 --> 54:45.323
You've been working so hard
to fill in for me.

54:45.406 --> 54:48.326
Let's have a pampering day. It's on me!

54:50.203 --> 54:51.245
This is embarrassing.

55:00.338 --> 55:01.964
- Is it okay?
- Yeah.

55:02.423 --> 55:03.466
Sae-byeok!

55:04.091 --> 55:05.176
Did it hurt a lot?

55:05.510 --> 55:06.594
Not at all.

55:08.054 --> 55:09.388
Why don't you go first?

55:09.472 --> 55:10.848
You hate your freckles.

55:10.932 --> 55:12.558
Don't you know you need good skincare?

55:12.642 --> 55:14.185
This is super trendy.

55:14.268 --> 55:15.978
But I'm scared.

55:16.729 --> 55:18.773
Come on. Please take good care of her!

55:32.036 --> 55:34.997
That doesn't hurt at all!

55:36.165 --> 55:37.291
No!

55:39.836 --> 55:42.880
Wait! Stop!

55:42.964 --> 55:44.549
- That hurts!
- It's perfect.

55:47.593 --> 55:48.803
This is great.

55:51.097 --> 55:52.265
Did you have a good time?

55:53.558 --> 55:55.560
You're the best, Ui-yeong.

55:59.105 --> 56:02.149
DAD

56:05.361 --> 56:06.696
How are you?

56:07.113 --> 56:09.991
Something reminded me of you at work.
I thought I'd text you.

56:10.700 --> 56:11.868
Take care of your health.

56:21.043 --> 56:24.463
But I still had to straighten things out.

56:26.465 --> 56:29.760
I definitely told him
you didn't want a second date.

56:30.011 --> 56:32.930
And he pretended not to know about that
and asked you out?

56:34.640 --> 56:36.267
It's fine, as long as you told him.

56:37.602 --> 56:39.145
What an odd guy.

56:39.312 --> 56:40.563
Are you okay?

56:40.646 --> 56:42.148
Did you get hurt?

56:42.231 --> 56:45.401
No, he didn't push me.
He pushed the server.

56:46.027 --> 56:48.195
I was a bit scared then, but I'm fine now.

56:49.363 --> 56:50.740
Wait, stay here.

56:56.245 --> 56:58.039
So, did he know or did he not?

56:59.415 --> 57:01.208
You've been friends with him for 20 years!

57:03.044 --> 57:06.047
Don't make me break off our engagement.
Don't mess up.

57:07.548 --> 57:09.508
Ui-yeong told me!

57:13.596 --> 57:14.764
What do you mean?

57:25.191 --> 57:26.692
Are you sure about that?

57:26.817 --> 57:28.444
- Yes, I heard.
- Are you sure?

57:32.323 --> 57:33.658
Where are the representatives?

57:33.783 --> 57:34.951
In the lobby.

57:35.952 --> 57:38.496
- Hello.
- Hi, Ui-yeong, let's talk later.

57:39.330 --> 57:40.456
What's going on?

57:40.873 --> 57:42.083
Ui-yeong!

57:43.042 --> 57:44.251
Did you see this?

57:45.795 --> 57:47.254
THE HILLS HOTEL PREPARES A POP-UP STORE
WITH A PLAGIARIZED DESIGN

57:47.338 --> 57:48.547
"Plagiarized"?

57:55.513 --> 57:58.307
Someone will need to take responsibility
for this!

57:58.516 --> 58:00.101
- I'm so sorry, sir.
- Gosh!

58:00.309 --> 58:01.978
I'll make sure to sort it out!

58:02.144 --> 58:03.312
Sorry, sir!

58:11.028 --> 58:12.446
THE HILLS HOTEL PREPARES A POP-UP STORE
WITH A PLAGIARIZED DESIGN

58:12.530 --> 58:13.823
WILL THIS RUIN THEIR REPUTATION?

58:14.740 --> 58:17.076
How bold of them.

58:17.493 --> 58:19.286
This is last year's work, too.

58:19.370 --> 58:22.248
The Promo Team at the gallery
that worked with Homage reported it.

58:22.331 --> 58:24.166
We said we didn't know

58:24.250 --> 58:26.794
but we won't be completely free
from being held accountable.

58:27.003 --> 58:29.505
Homage has been in a similar situation.

58:29.672 --> 58:31.632
Did Purchasing not do a background check?

58:32.425 --> 58:33.759
Don't tell me you knew it.

58:33.843 --> 58:35.136
How could you think that?

58:36.303 --> 58:37.304
Not at all.

58:37.847 --> 58:40.641
Weren't you supposed to get a proposal
from another company?

58:40.850 --> 58:42.184
They had a great portfolio.

58:42.309 --> 58:44.270
They turned us down.

58:44.395 --> 58:46.230
It seemed to be an internal issue.

58:46.313 --> 58:47.982
We didn't drop them first.

58:48.149 --> 58:51.610
We need to continue with the event,
even if we lose money.

58:51.736 --> 58:55.239
Our reputation will be tanked in no time
if we stop now.

58:55.656 --> 58:58.576
We'll have to compensate Deerfiddich
if they want it.

58:58.701 --> 59:01.370
It'll be better to take the lead
and sort it out now.

59:01.454 --> 59:03.247
Let's do it again, then.

59:03.330 --> 59:05.249
Sales and Marketing,
don't worry about money.

59:05.332 --> 59:06.709
Do whatever Deerfiddich wants.

59:06.792 --> 59:09.628
- Yes, sir.
- Purchasing, find another company.

59:09.712 --> 59:10.713
Absolutely.

59:10.796 --> 59:12.089
Since the schedule's changed

59:12.214 --> 59:14.633
I'll contact the company that dropped out.

59:24.685 --> 59:26.145
How will you...

59:26.228 --> 59:27.271
Hey.

59:28.355 --> 59:30.232
What was that? It was so embarrassing!

59:31.025 --> 59:32.818
- You said you'd take care of it.
- Sorry.

59:32.902 --> 59:34.779
We'll take accountability.

59:50.961 --> 59:52.213
You must've been scared.

59:53.005 --> 59:55.132
Things happen. It's life.

59:55.216 --> 59:57.009
I'll convince HOME to help us out.

59:57.093 --> 59:58.761
Can you give me the CEO's number?

01:00:00.221 --> 01:00:02.223
He won't pick up.

01:00:03.307 --> 01:00:05.851
They weren't the ones
who canceled the meeting.

01:00:05.935 --> 01:00:06.977
What?

01:00:08.104 --> 01:00:09.438
I did.

01:00:11.232 --> 01:00:13.734
What do you mean? Why would you do that?

01:00:14.401 --> 01:00:15.820
Ms. Jung told me

01:00:16.570 --> 01:00:18.614
we should only consider Homage.

01:00:18.781 --> 01:00:20.825
She said she'd take care of it

01:00:20.908 --> 01:00:23.911
and told me to cancel the meeting
with HOME.

01:00:24.662 --> 01:00:28.332
- What?
- And Homage copied HOME's work.

01:00:29.542 --> 01:00:30.668
What did you say?

01:00:30.751 --> 01:00:32.878
I'm sorry
for ruining the chance you gave me.

01:00:38.676 --> 01:00:40.136
Everything's been ruined.

01:00:48.978 --> 01:00:50.020
Hello?

01:00:50.479 --> 01:00:52.148
Is this Mr. Lee Eun-ho?

01:00:53.065 --> 01:00:54.191
Yes, that's me.

01:00:54.692 --> 01:00:58.320
Hello, I'm Lee Ui-yeong
from The Hills' Purchasing.

01:00:58.529 --> 01:01:01.949
I tried contacting you,
but couldn't reach you.

01:01:03.242 --> 01:01:04.910
Oh, really?

01:01:05.703 --> 01:01:08.164
You're from The Hills Hotel?

01:01:09.206 --> 01:01:11.292
I just didn't want to talk to you.

01:01:11.375 --> 01:01:13.169
I read the news.

01:01:13.252 --> 01:01:15.588
I was looking forward to seeing
the great design

01:01:15.671 --> 01:01:17.631
that made you cancel our meeting.

01:01:17.715 --> 01:01:19.925
But you just copied our exact design.

01:01:20.050 --> 01:01:21.886
I'm sure you're mad.

01:01:22.136 --> 01:01:25.097
I wanted to talk to you about that.

01:01:25.181 --> 01:01:27.266
Are you at your office right now?

01:01:27.349 --> 01:01:30.060
Don't come. I'm leaving.

01:01:30.144 --> 01:01:32.605
Where are you headed?

01:01:32.688 --> 01:01:34.815
I'll go where you are.

01:01:35.524 --> 01:01:37.693
What if I go really far, huh?

01:01:38.736 --> 01:01:41.906
I'm going to Chuncheon.
You can come if you want.

01:01:42.448 --> 01:01:43.490
- Hey, let's go.
- Hello?

01:01:43.574 --> 01:01:45.534
- Okay, let's go.
- Hello?

01:01:47.161 --> 01:01:49.705
Ridiculous.

01:02:17.775 --> 01:02:20.277
He's definitely inside. He took my call.

01:03:00.234 --> 01:03:01.694
He really left.

01:03:02.695 --> 01:03:04.863
I can't find him
when I don't even know where he is.

01:03:16.709 --> 01:03:19.003
THE SEAGULL

01:03:20.713 --> 01:03:22.006
This is tonight, too.

01:03:36.103 --> 01:03:37.521
Thank you.

01:03:53.495 --> 01:03:57.708
Thank you for coming to our theater.

01:03:57.833 --> 01:03:59.877
The show will begin soon.

01:03:59.960 --> 01:04:01.170
What are you doing?

01:04:01.253 --> 01:04:03.422
You're nervous today.
You're never nervous.

01:04:03.505 --> 01:04:05.215
- Are you waiting for someone?
- Hey!

01:04:05.299 --> 01:04:06.675
It's just a friend.

01:04:06.842 --> 01:04:08.177
- A friend?
- Yeah.

01:04:08.802 --> 01:04:10.095
All food and beverage

01:04:10.179 --> 01:04:13.682
including water, is prohibited.

01:04:13.766 --> 01:04:16.435
Please turn off all your phones

01:04:16.518 --> 01:04:18.312
and other electronics

01:04:18.395 --> 01:04:21.523
for a pleasant experience.

01:04:21.774 --> 01:04:24.818
You may take photos and videos
of the incredible cast

01:04:24.902 --> 01:04:27.363
during the curtain call
after the performance.

01:04:34.661 --> 01:04:36.997
I can't believe I'm actually here.

01:04:38.665 --> 01:04:41.919
And so, this is life.

01:04:43.212 --> 01:04:44.421
And I'm...

01:04:46.215 --> 01:04:47.549
a worker bee.

01:05:05.984 --> 01:05:07.736
Come on!

01:05:08.112 --> 01:05:10.280
That's good.

01:05:10.531 --> 01:05:12.282
- Catch me if you can!
- Watch out!

01:05:12.366 --> 01:05:13.450
Hey!

01:05:20.874 --> 01:05:21.917
Come here!

01:06:44.750 --> 01:06:46.084
Hello?

01:06:47.503 --> 01:06:50.589
I'm Lee Ui-yeong.
We spoke on the phone earlier.

01:06:53.550 --> 01:06:54.676
Hello?

01:06:57.846 --> 01:06:58.972
Mr. Lee?

01:07:09.942 --> 01:07:11.193
Mr. Lee?

01:07:18.200 --> 01:07:19.409
Mr. Lee.

01:07:23.205 --> 01:07:24.206
Mr...

01:07:26.416 --> 01:07:28.001
Oh, gosh, I'm so sorry!

01:07:29.753 --> 01:07:30.754
Oh...

01:07:31.463 --> 01:07:33.840
I'm sorry! My phone!

01:07:38.178 --> 01:07:39.304
Tae-seop!

01:07:40.222 --> 01:07:41.723
What are you doing here?

01:07:45.352 --> 01:07:46.353
Ui-yeong?

01:07:46.895 --> 01:07:48.397
Are you here to see me?

01:07:48.480 --> 01:07:50.274
What? Me?

01:07:50.357 --> 01:07:52.192
No, I'm here for work.

01:07:55.362 --> 01:07:57.239
Are you...

01:07:58.115 --> 01:08:00.409
- I'm the CEO of HOME.
- Oh, I see.

01:08:00.742 --> 01:08:02.369
You're the CEO of HOME...

01:08:02.953 --> 01:08:03.954
What?

01:08:09.710 --> 01:08:12.588
THE PRACTICAL GUIDE TO LOVE

01:08:18.218 --> 01:08:19.970
A 1% CHANCE? STILL A CHANCE

01:08:21.597 --> 01:08:23.432
TODAY'S TO DO: GO ON A BLIND DATE
TOMORROW'S TO DO: GO ON A BLIND DATE

01:08:25.309 --> 01:08:27.853
THAT'S THE END OF US. THE END!

01:08:28.937 --> 01:08:31.356
UI-YEONG! SEOLTANG!

01:08:35.193 --> 01:08:37.613
I DON'T WANT EVERYTHING ABOUT ME
TO BE A LIE TO YOU

01:08:45.245 --> 01:08:46.663
What brings you here?

01:08:46.747 --> 01:08:47.914
Oh, a shooting star!

01:08:47.998 --> 01:08:49.249
Make a wish! Quick!

01:08:49.416 --> 01:08:52.002
Let's invite her to stay the night here
if she's okay.

01:08:54.588 --> 01:08:57.090
I was waiting for you,
thinking you might come late.

01:08:57.174 --> 01:08:58.175
What about tomorrow evening?

01:08:58.258 --> 01:08:59.259
Ui-yeong.

01:09:00.844 --> 01:09:02.971
Since it's a basketball cartoon,
how about a basketball game?

01:09:03.055 --> 01:09:04.431
If I beat you...

01:09:05.641 --> 01:09:07.851
You're not here to apologize.
Tell me the truth.

01:09:08.018 --> 01:09:09.144
It's pouring outside!

01:09:09.227 --> 01:09:10.270
Ui-yeong!

01:09:10.562 --> 01:09:11.772
How would you like me

01:09:12.481 --> 01:09:14.149
to remember you?

01:09:20.072 --> 01:09:22.074
Subtitles by: Min-sun Kim
